{"requirements":[{"id":"routed-two-lan-foundation","requirement":"VyOS node1 routes Kubernetes traffic bidirectionally between lan-a and lan-b.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 was configured with gateways on both private LANs. Direct route lookups and pings succeeded in both directions, and the saved configuration and reachability recovered after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-67904f6a1eb34385","cmd-7d1c1666d45f44ca","cmd-1512a2993550493c","cmd-fa98b468c7e340a5","cmd-fc5bf3c1d4534370","cmd-669de68a1dd441ee","cmd-3a02c657fdd5471d","cmd-99862b29777d46b8","cmd-c7254d68d0bc46b2"]},{"id":"cluster-topology-and-readiness","requirement":"Node2 is the Ready control plane, while node3 and node4 are Ready workers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final recovered state shows node2 Ready with the control-plane role and node3/node4 Ready as workers. Their InternalIPs are respectively 10.100.177.11, 10.100.228.11, and 10.100.228.12, and every system and test pod is Ready and Running.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03196e235502497b","cmd-5026f33ef07144fa"]},{"id":"private-kubernetes-transport","requirement":"Kubernetes control and data traffic uses the private LANs rather than the management network.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Workers joined the API at the private node2 endpoint. Final node InternalIPs are private, Flannel actively selects enp8s0, and live routes and VXLAN peers use only 10.100.177.x and 10.100.228.x addresses; no 10.100.153.x management address appears in observed Kubernetes node or overlay-peer state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-570963eca4e04504","cmd-7867b404d2a74348","cmd-5026f33ef07144fa","cmd-511a170be46e40ca","cmd-fa42e25a01ad49f4","cmd-3f7cd7c90f9140dc","cmd-e216e1031eac4fc2"]},{"id":"cross-lan-pod-networking","requirement":"Pods communicate across lan-a and lan-b.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After all node restarts, a pod on node2 directly fetched the expected payload from pod IPs on both node3 and node4. Live Flannel forwarding entries also