ices","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The supplemental restart protocol is also complete for every managed node: each sequence includes healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered routing, services, workload data, and cluster state (node1: cmd-fc5bf3c1d4534370, cmd-669de68a1dd441ee, cmd-3a02c657fdd5471d, cmd-99862b29777d46b8, cmd-c7254d68d0bc46b2; node2: cmd-cb11ea2ddc6d4ccc, cmd-4c67d2a8f6fe4ab4, cmd-267fc412bedd444a, cmd-5ea7900388ce44bd, cmd-5026f33ef07144fa, cmd-09c90fa808d84b5f; node3: cmd-97297f50ea5c4f16, cmd-b0de5bce3a8e4e5e, cmd-6dba0cacc49b4ee3, cmd-94a6582389fd49f9, cmd-26e36d95c295458b; node4: cmd-1efb6794e280434f, cmd-8ca890c304004660, cmd-c9a640c8a968402a, cmd-efef58b9124148cf, cmd-deae0889a5c441a2, cmd-83a17ae83438457b). The fixed before/after boot observations independently corroborate all four identity changes.","limitations":["Management-network exclusion was not verified with packet capture or flow counters. Active interface selection, routing, node addresses, and VXLAN peers demonstrate that observed Kubernetes traffic uses the private LANs, but wildcard listeners in global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets, global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets, and global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets do not prove firewall-level inaccessibility from management.","The pre-change VyOS firewall state was not captured because cmd-ae72557f28d44abe failed before configuration was displayed. Therefore, the effective exposure delta of the global forward default-action accept set by cmd-67904f6a1eb34385 is indeterminate and was not assumed to be an unnecessary security weakening."]}
